{
  "kind": "vocabulary",
  "name": "biped",
  "about": "Poses, cycles and expressions keyed on the standard biped part names (4.0 K3). Joints are degrees on the 2 degree grid from the part's rest; an -l limb turned positive and an -r limb turned negative swing out and up (out to their side in the front view, the far one back and the near one forward in profile); in profile every limb turned negative swings forward. A variant may be a list: the first one the puppet has wins. 'top' and 'mid' mean a puppet's last and middle mouth. A pose or cycle applies to a puppet that has every part in its `needs` and keeps at least one key; the rest are dropped by the actor's known(). `body` is the trunk above the hips: a puppet whose body is its root does not take its turns. `views` is the view each pose and cycle is drawn for (front when not named). A frame's lift is the stage's (4% of the figure's height), not the puppet's units.",
  "names": ["head", "neck", "body", "hips", "arm-l", "arm-r", "fore-l", "fore-r", "hand-l", "hand-r", "leg-l", "leg-r", "shin-l", "shin-r", "foot-l", "foot-r", "eye", "pupil", "brow-l", "brow-r", "mouth", "tail"],
